This repository contain Verilog code for the design of a driver for a 7 segment display. This display shows the outputs of a 4 bit full adder and their carry based on the selector switch.
Instructions:

1.Create project in Vivaldo using correct FPGA selected
2.Move display driver code into source file
3.Assign inputs to switches and segments on FPGA usings provided file
4.Add constraint to add test bench 
5.Run Simulation to check wave form (Test bench should show corresponding value for seg of the additions)
6.Run synthesis and check resulting gate level results
7.Create bit stream
8.Program FPGA
9.Test FPGA with sample inputs of a=5 and b = 3. Should yield 8 on display
